===== README.md =====
executable: false

# `npm-minimal`

[![npm version](https://img.shields.io/npm/v/npm-minimal.svg)](https://www.npmjs.com/package/npm-minimal)
[![License: UNLICENSED](https://img.shields.io/badge/license-UNLICENSED-blue.svg)](LICENSE)

A TypeScript library.

## Install

```bash
npm install npm-minimal
```

## Usage

```ts
import { formatValue } from "npm-minimal";

const output = formatValue({ ready: true });
```

## Development

Lint, format, type-check, dependency and security policy checks, and tests are
wired into a single command:

```bash
npm run check         # lint + dep/security checks + typecheck + coverage
npm run test          # run tests
npm run build         # build to dist/
npm run release:check # package validation + publish dry run
```

`npm run security:lint` prefers `semgrep` on PATH and otherwise runs the pinned `uvx semgrep@1.165.0` scan.

See [`AGENTS.md`](AGENTS.md) for the conventions this project follows.

## License

[UNLICENSED](LICENSE) © Unknown Author.

